@_jmwebb Natural fermentation is much preferrable over protein powders

"Most commercial protein powders are technically classified as ultra-processed foods (UPFs) under systems like NOVA because they involve industrial isolation of nutrients and often contain additives like artificial sweeteners, emulsifiers, and thickeners. However, unlike junk food UPFs, they are functional supplements meant to deliver targeted nutrients rather than empty calories"

"No, natural skyr is not an ultra-processed food. It is a traditional fermented dairy product made with just pasteurized skimmed milk and live active cultures (and sometimes a microbial coagulant/rennet), then strained to remove the whey. This simple, traditional method places it in the processed or minimally processed category, not the ultra-processed category"

